      "evidence_type": "LEXICAL_CANDIDATE",
      "excerpt": "            <p> However, there might be situations where once a long running task starts execution, its heartbeats might fail repeatedly yet the task execution continues. ATF would retry this task by polling it from the store consumer because the heartbeat timeouts would’ve expired. This task can then be claimed by another worker and lead to concurrent execution.&#160;<br />"
